        <div class="row">
            
       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <!-- Blog Main Content Here -->
             <!-- Use class 'blog-content' for the wrapper -->
             <!-- CRITICAL: The main image MUST have src="data:image/jpeg;base64," -->
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Karnataka School Examination and Assessment Board 1st PUC Result 2026">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026 Declared: Your Gateway to 2nd PUC!</h1>

                    <p>The wait is finally over for over 6.8 lakh students across Karnataka! The Karnataka School Examination and Assessment Board (KSEAB) has officially declared the 1st PUC (Pre-University Course) results for the academic year 2025-26. Students who appeared for the Class 11 examinations can now access their provisional mark sheets online and take the next step in their academic journey. This comprehensive guide will walk you through everything you need to know about checking your KSEAB 1st PUC Result 2026, understanding your marks, and important next steps.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Key Highlights of KSEAB 1st PUC Result 2026</h2>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ <strong>Results Declared:</strong> Most schools saw results on March 30, 2026, with Dakshina Kannada District results released on March 31, 2026.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Official Websites:</strong> Results are available on result.proed.in, kseab.karnataka.gov.in, and result.bspucpa.in.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Required Credentials:</strong> Students need their Registration Number (or SATS Number) and Date of Birth to check scores.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Provisional Mark Sheet:</strong> The online result is provisional; original mark sheets will be issued by colleges.</p>
                        <p>✅ <strong>Passing Criteria:</strong> A minimum of 35% marks in each subject is required to pass the examination.</p>
                    </div>

                    <p class="highlight-text">The KSEAB 1st PUC examinations for the 2025-26 academic year were successfully conducted between February 28 and March 17, 2026, across various streams including Science, Commerce, and Arts.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026 Online</h2>
                    <p>Accessing your KSEAB 1st PUC results is a straightforward process. Follow these step-by-step instructions to download your provisional marks memo:</p>
                    
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Results Portal</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Open your web browser and navigate to one of the official Karnataka results websites: <a href="https://result.proed.in" target="_blank">result.proed.in</a>, <a href="https://kseab.karnataka.gov.in" target="_blank">kseab.karnataka.gov.in</a>, or <a href="https://result.bspucpa.in" target="_blank">result.bspucpa.in</a>.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for the link specifically for "Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026" or "1st PUC Annual Exam Result 2026". Click on it.</div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">You will be redirected to a new page where you need to enter your login details. Carefully input your Registration Number (or SATS Number) and your Date of Birth.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">4. Submit and View Result</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">After entering the required information, click on the "Submit" or "Go" button. Your Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026 will then be displayed on your screen.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">5. Download and Print</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Review your marks and details. It is highly recommended to download the marksheet PDF and take a printout for your records and future reference. Remember, this is a provisional document.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Important Details on Your Marksheet</h2>
                    <p>Your provisional KSEAB 1st PUC mark sheet will contain several crucial pieces of information:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Student's Name</p>
                        <p>✅ Registration Number / Roll Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Name of Examination (1st PUC 2026)</p>
                        <p>✅ Board Name (KSEAB)</p>
                        <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks</p>
                        <p>✅ Total Marks Obtained</p>
                        <p>✅ Qualifying Status (Pass/Fail)</p>
                        <p>✅ Stream (Science/Commerce/Arts)</p>
                        <p>✅ School/College Name</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">What's Next? Re-evaluation and Supplementary Exams</h2>
                    <p>For students who may not be satisfied with their results or have not cleared all subjects, KSEAB provides options for re-evaluation and supplementary examinations.</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">Re-evaluation and Scrutiny</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">If you believe there might have been an error in the evaluation of your answer scripts, you can apply for re-evaluation or re-checking. The official notification regarding the application dates and procedures will be released by KSEAB soon. Keep an eye on the official website for these announcements.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">Supplementary Examinations</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Students who unfortunately did not secure passing marks in one or more subjects are eligible to appear for the Karnataka 1st PUC Supplementary Exams 2026. While the official schedule is yet to be announced, based on previous trends, these exams are typically conducted in the months following the main result, often around late May. This offers a valuable second chance to clear the subjects and progress to 2nd PUC.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Key Dates at a Glance</h2>
                    <p>Here's a summary of important dates related to the Karnataka 1st PUC Result 2026:</p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Event</th>
                                <th>Date/Period</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>1st PUC Examinations (2025-26)</td>
                                <td>February 28 - March 17, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>1st PUC Result Declaration (Most Schools)</td>
                                <td>March 30, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>1st PUC Result Declaration (Dakshina Kannada District)</td>
                                <td>March 31, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Online Result Access Begins</td>
                                <td>March 31, 2026 (from 9:25 AM / 10:00 AM)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Application for Re-evaluation/Scrutiny</td>
                                <td>To be announced</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>Supplementary Examinations</td>
                                <td>Expected May 2026 (based on past trends)</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <p>Congratulations to all the students who successfully cleared their Karnataka 1st PUC exams! For those who need to utilize the re-evaluation or supplementary exam options, remember to stay positive and prepare thoroughly. Keep checking the official KSEAB website for all the latest updates and notifications. Your journey to 2nd PUC awaits!</p>
                </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
